## 2. Two-Tier Hierarchical Approval Workflow Engine

Per the governance requirement: *"whatever they do using this tool should be approved by their line managers and their work in turn needs to be approved by their line managers."*

```mermaid
sequenceDiagram
    autonumber
    actor PM as Project Manager<br/>(e.g., Arpit Mathur)
    actor LM1 as Line Manager [SPM]<br/>(e.g., Aashna Arora)
    actor LM2 as Supervising Leader [Director/PA]<br/>(e.g., Subroto Ghosh)
    actor SG as Secretary General<br/>(Chakravarthy T. Kannan)
    actor Admin as System Admin<br/>(Prabhav Kumar Singh)

    Note over PM: Uses RAG Draft Generation<br/>for new Work Order / Extension
    PM->>PM: Create Draft (Status: DRAFT)
    PM->>LM1: Submit for Line Approval (Status: PENDING_L1_REVIEW)

    alt Line Manager Requests Changes
        LM1-->>PM: Rejection / Request Revision with comments (Status: REJECTED)
        PM->>LM1: Resubmit modified draft
    else Line Manager Approves
        LM1->>LM2: Approve Level 1 (Status: APPROVED_L1_PENDING_L2)
    end

    alt Supervising Leader Approves
        LM2->>LM2: Approve Level 2 (Status: FINAL_APPROVED)
        Note over LM2,SG: Document officially published to Institutional Archive
    else Supervising Leader Rejects
        LM2-->>PM: Send back with executive notes (Status: REJECTED)
    end

    Note over SG,Admin: SG & Admin receive real-time dashboard notifications<br/>and maintain full audit visibility across all phases
```

### State Machine Definition:
1. `DRAFT`: Initiated by PM or SPM using RAG / template tool.
2. `PENDING_L1_REVIEW`: Submitted to direct Line Manager (N+1).
3. `APPROVED_L1_PENDING_L2`: Approved by Line Manager; routed automatically to Line Manager's Manager (N+2).
4. `FINAL_APPROVED`: Approved by Supervising Director/Advisor; stamped with cryptographic verification and stored in the institutional repository.
5. `REJECTED`: Returned to initiator with comments and tracked revision history.

